  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read it",
      "items": [
        "A box is a thread: the main thread, a pool's worker, an own worker or the bus worker. A card inside it is one isolate or a group of isolates, with the count on the card.",
        "T3 is shown in full and stands for every machine; T1, T2 and T4\u2013T8 are grouped.",
        "Arrows show records published to and delivered from each topic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "When something blocks",
      "items": [
        "The kernel kills a thread whose loop stays busy past 2 s and restarts it with every isolate on it.",
        "In split, only that machine's 8 widgets stall; data keeps flowing.",
        "Restarted isolates read their topics back from the start: 2 minutes of slow signals."
      ]
    }
  ]
